  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1202 PM CDT Wed Jul 29 2026\n\nUnfortunately for those who are ready for a break from the heat, I \ndo not have the best news to report as we expect this triple digit \nheat to continue through Friday. However the good news (sort of?) is \nthat we will see a slight cool down through the weekend (laughable) \nwith chances for precipitation returning (yay!) by Friday. The \npersistent upper ridge and associated area of high pressure will \nremain the dominate synoptic feature through the end of the week \ninto the weekend, while monsoonal moisture continues to wrap around \nits eastern periphery. At the same time, a shortwave trough \ntransversing across the Upper Midwest into the Great Lakes region \nwill drive a weak cold front southward into the forecast area late \nFriday. The front, combined with increased layer (H3-H8) moisture \nand weak large scale ascent will support low chances for showers and \nthunderstorms through the weekend. Confidence in coverage and timing \nremains low at this time, with widespread actively being dependent \non FROPA timing, in combination with the influence of the ridge. \nHowever, the good news is that we can expect temperatures to cool a \nfew degrees, into the 90s, through the weekend. Thereafter, the warm \nand drier trend returns, as the upper level ridge expands eastward \nsuppressing precipitation chances while temperatures climb back into \nthe triple digits.",
